  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef la_qr_decomposition(matrix: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **QR Decomposition** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef la_qr_decomposition(matrix: list) -> dict:\n    Q, R = np.linalg.qr(np.array(matrix, dtype=np.float64))\n    return {'Q': np.round(Q, 6).tolist(), 'R': np.round(R, 6).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
